          "where": "Mission Concept & Rationale",
          "quote": "A near-real-time relay to monitoring stations on the ground would allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching events."
        },
        {
          "where": "Mission Concept & Rationale",
          "quote": "This tool could be applied to a new satellite over the Great Barrier Reef."
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": "The need, broad mission function, Australian benefit, and intended users are identifiable, with supporting sources. The concept lacks specific mission requirements and payload or service performance targets, so it is only at the lower end of Accomplished."
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "level": "Adequate",
      "mark": 5,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "where": "Project Plan & Preliminary Progress",
          "quote": "Project work will be divided into weeks via a Gantt Chart."
        },
        {
          "where": "Project Plan & Preliminary Progress",
          "quote": "Running basic simulations in STK will also be useful."
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": "A Gantt chart and task descriptions make the plan broadly feasible and connect planned work to launch, orbit, and mission design. However, contingency planning is absent, some timing descriptions conflict with the chart, and planned information sources are not clearly set out."
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "level": "Adequate",
      "mark": 4,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "where": "Project Plan & Preliminary Progress",
          "quote": "I have read the brief of Asner’s monitoring system in Hawaii, researched into how coral bleaching occurs and its severity, and also completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4."
        },
        {
          "where": "Project Plan & Preliminary Progress",
          "quote": "My current choice is a geostationary orbit at an altitude of 600 km"
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": "Research and software tutorials constitute some preliminary work, but no useful technical results, calculations, or interpreted simulations are presented. The proposed orbit is technically inconsistent: a 600 km orbit is not geostationary."
    },
    {
      "id": "C4",
      "level": "Adequate",
      "mark": 5,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "where": "Mission Concept & Rationale",
          "quote": "Coral reefs, specifically the Great Barrier Reef, would immensely benefit from dedicated satellite monitoring."
        },
        {
          "where": "Project Plan & Preliminary Progress",
          "quote": "Detailed task descriptions can be found on the next page."
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": "Headings, coherent sections, and a legible labelled Gantt chart support readability. Some phrasing is informal or awkward, and the references are presented as numbered URLs rather than a complete reference list. The plan's prose and chart also have some inconsistencies."
    }
