  "technical_issues": [
    {
      "where": "Project Plan & Preliminary Progress",
      "issue": "A 600 km altitude orbit cannot be geostationary. Geostationary orbit requires an approximately 35,786 km altitude circular, equatorial orbit with a 24-hour period; a low orbit would not remain fixed over the reef."
    },
    {
      "where": "Project Plan & Preliminary Progress",
      "issue": "The plan says final simulations should be completed by the end of week 9, while the chart shows STK simulations scheduled through week 10."
    }
  ],
  "overall": "The report presents a relevant Australian mission concept, a timetable, and evidence of initial research and STK learning. Its main weaknesses are limited preliminary engineering results, incomplete identification of planned information sources, and a fundamental error in the proposed orbit. The mission concept is promising but needs quantified requirements and a feasible orbit strategy."
